# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
"""Encyclopedia descriptions, batch K (DeepSeek)."""
DESC_K = {
    'PT': {
        141: "Rosamia was a cyber-newtype trained at the Augusta Research Institute, holding the nominal rank of lieutenant. She lost her family in a colony drop during the One Year War, and her trauma was exploited for mental enhancement. However, the repeated experiments and enhancements caused her mind to become unstable. She was assigned to Bran's unit and fought Kamille numerous times in her Gaplant.",
        142: "Four was a cyber-newtype trained at the Murasame Research Institute and the pilot of the Psyco Gundam, holding the nominal rank of lieutenant. Ordinarily gentle and mild-mannered, when she boarded the Psyco Gundam she came under the influence of its mental control waves, transforming into a violent personality accompanied by intense headaches. She had lost her memories of the past, and this deep-seated complex bound her tightly. The name Four was not her real name; it merely marked her as the fourth test subject at the Murasame Institute. Yet she believed the words that destroying the Gundam Mk-II would restore her memories, and endured her headaches to remain in the Psyco Gundam's cockpit. Meeting Kamille let her touch the warmth of the human heart, but learning that he was the Gundam Mk-II's pilot brought her great anguish.",
        143: 'Mauar was a Titans officer of seventeen, holding the rank of lieutenant. She met Jerid while escaping from Jaburo, and as they worked together she came to love him and his abilities. She possessed solid piloting skill backed by calm judgment and initiative. Scirocco recognized her potential, but she saw him as a danger and refused his offer. She continued to support Jerid unwaveringly as he burned to defeat Kamille.',
        144: "Yazan was a Titans officer, initially a lieutenant and later promoted to captain. He had a belligerent personality and genuinely enjoyed war, where he could wield his strength freely. As a pilot he showed exceptional skill, handling high-mobility mobile suits such as the Gaplant and Hambrabi like extensions of his own body, and repeatedly harried the Argama's mobile suit team. He possessed the cunning and cruelty to murder even a superior officer without hesitation if it suited his purposes. Yet he also had a caring side, and seemed to be trusted deeply by subordinates such as Ramsus and Dunkel.",
        145: 'Dunkel was a Titans officer and a member of the Hambrabi squadron commanded by Yazan. His skill as a pilot was solid, and through coordinated attacks he troubled the Argama on numerous occasions.',
        146: 'Ramsus Hasa was an officer of the Titans and a member of the Hambrabi unit commanded by Yazan. Though coarse in personality, he possessed solid skill as a pilot. This can be seen from the fact that Yazan trusted him enough to recruit him as a subordinate and entrust him with a new model mobile suit.\n\nHis rough nature did not hinder his competence, and his reliability in battle made him a valued asset within the unit.',
        147: 'Sara Zabirov was a Newtype candidate of the Titans. Her rank was sergeant. She was drawn to Scirocco, who acknowledged her, and swore absolute loyalty to him. Though the words of Kamille and Katz moved her heart, she never left his side.\n\nHer devotion remained unwavering even as she wrestled with the doubts they planted in her mind.',
        148: "Paptimus Scirocco was the captain of the Jupiter ship Jupitris, leading the Jupiter fleet of the Earth Federation government. His rank was lieutenant commander. He was 26 years old. He possessed high Newtype abilities and charisma. Furthermore, he was a genius who perfectly handled everything from mobile suit design to piloting, operational planning and command, and even the handling of women. This power charmed Sara, caused Reccoa to defect from the AEUG, and even brought the highly selective Yazan over to his side.\n\nHe openly stated that 'after the war, women will rule the world,' but the meaning of these words remained unclear to the end. After returning to the Earth sphere, he belonged to the Titans, but the ambition born of his talent seemed not to fit within the framework of the military.",
        149: 'Basque Om was the right-hand man of Jamitov, who founded the Titans, and was in effect the supreme commander of military operations. His rank was colonel. He was 37 years old. To compensate for his weakened eyesight, he always wore goggles like underwater swimming glasses. It was said this came from the aftereffects of torture suffered when he was captured by the Principality of Zeon forces during the One Year War.\n\nHe had a cruel personality that showed no mercy to anyone other than the Titans, especially Spacenoids. He would not hesitate to use poison gas against colonies or take hostages to recover the Gundam Mk-II, choosing any means to achieve his goals. He was truly a man who symbolized the Titans.',
        150: "Jamaican Daninghan was an officer of the Titans and Basque's close confidant. His rank was major. He was of a superior class as a commander, but he was a believer in elitist ideology and had an arrogant personality. In reality, however, he was a coward who only watched his superiors' expressions, and so it seemed he did not enjoy the trust of his subordinates.",
        151: 'Jamitov Hymem is a founding member of the Titans and its current supreme commander, holding the rank of General. He is a dangerous man who, while hostile toward Spacenoids, even considers purging the Earthnoids who pollute the Earth. He made the Titans his own personal tool for this purpose, but it is ironic that those who disapproved of his high-handed methods joined forces and gave rise to the AEUG, his greatest obstacle. He had long been at odds with the AEUG leader Blex as a political rival. While having his confidant Basque command the Titans, he deliberately released the dangerous element Scirocco within the organization to stir up activity.',
        152: "Gady Kinsey is an officer of the Titans and captain of the cruiser Alexandria. He is a soldier's soldier who values discipline, and his meticulous nature leads him to speak his mind even to superiors if they overstep their authority.",
        153: "Wong Lee is an executive of Anaheim Electronics. Entrusted with full authority by the company's chairman, Melanie, he is the man monitoring the AEUG aboard the Argama. Compared to the TV version, where he left a strong impression of correcting Kamille and the others at every turn, in the theatrical version he is portrayed as a strict but composed adult.",
        154: "Blex Forer is the representative of the anti-Earth Federation organization AEUG, holding the rank of Commodore. At 58 years old, he was a high-ranking official of the Earth Federation Forces and a member of the Earth Federation Assembly, but concerned over the rise of the Titans and policies that disregarded the Earth's environment, he organized the AEUG. He was a man of gentle character with a flexible mindset that showed understanding even toward Newtypes, and he held high hopes for Kamille.",
        155: "Henken Bekkener is a central figure of the AEUG, holding the rank of Lieutenant Colonel. He was the first captain of the Argama, but upon Bright's joining of the AEUG, he yielded that position and became captain of the Radish. Though he had spent many years in the military, he retained a certain human warmth that endeared him to his crew. He had also participated in the One Year War and was said to have felt the pressure of the Red Comet on the battlefield. He harbored feelings for Emma and often showed a sincere, boyish side.",
        156: "Astonaige Medos serves as the chief mechanic of the Argama, holding the rank of petty officer. His skill is assured given his position, and because of him, the Argama's mobile suit team is always able to fight at full readiness. In the TV version, he sent Kamille's ideas to Anaheim Electronics, playing a hidden role as a contributor to the completion of the Z Gundam. However, this aspect is not depicted in the theatrical version.",
        157: 'Hayato Kobayashi is the founder of Karaba, a support organization for the AEUG, and the captain of the Audhumla. He had been serving as the director of a war museum at Kennedy, but he rose up after witnessing the tyranny of the Titans. During the One Year War, he was a crew member of the White Base, and after the war ended, he married Frau and adopted the orphans Katz, Lets, and Kikka.',
        158: "Kai Shiden is ostensibly a freelance journalist (in his own words, 'little more than a tabloid hack'). In reality, however, he is a collaborator who provides information on the Titans to the AEUG and Karaba. During the One Year War, he had fought alongside Hayato on the White Base, and he would investigate the locations of Federation headquarters and relay them to Hayato. Nevertheless, he shows reluctance about fighting together with Quattro, knowing him to be Char.",
        159: 'Beltorchika Irma is a member of Karaba, a support organization for the AEUG. She is an energetic woman, but because she has a tendency to blurt out whatever she thinks, she often incurred the resentment of those around her. When she made contact with the Audhumla, she was delighted to meet Amuro, the hero of the One Year War, in whom she had been interested from before. She soon repeated intense overtures toward him, and eventually came to support the roused Amuro as his lover.',
        160: "Haman Karn is the regent of the resource asteroid Axis, where remnants of the Principality of Zeon's military have gathered. In practice, however, she is the leader who commands the entire force. Her personality is fierce and cold. Using Mineva, the orphaned child of Gihren Zabi, as her banner, she proclaimed the revival of Zeon and possessed the high political acumen to elevate Axis, once a minor power, into a major force. Her mobile suit piloting skill and her abilities as a Newtype are also high, and she sometimes takes to the front lines herself in dedicated machines such as the Gaza C and the Qubeley. She has a past history with Quattro, and harbors complex feelings toward him that could be called both love and hatred.",
        161: "The late Vice Admiral of the old Principality of Zeon, Dozle Zabi's orphaned child. Age 8.\nIn her youth, she has become a symbol of Zeon's restoration through the hands of her guardian, Haman. However, this is merely her authority as a puppet of Haman, and as a result, she has received a rather biased education.",
        162: "A Moonrace boy who pilots the Turn A Gundam. Age 17.\nAlong with Keith and Fran, he descended to Earth two years ago as an advance surveyor for the Earth return operation. At that time, he was saved from drowning in a river by the Heim sisters, and through that connection came to work at the Heim family's mine, eventually becoming a servant.\nHe is gentle and dislikes conflict, but in order to stop the war between the Moon and Earth, he reluctantly joined the Ingressa Militia.\nContrary to his personality, he excels at piloting mobile suits, and combined with the Turn A Gundam's performance, he played a central role in the Militia. Also, even in situations where he faced enemies on foot without a suit, he showed a manly side, fighting bravely without flinching.\nLike other Moonrace, he was devoted to Dianna, and his actions were always prioritized with Dianna in mind.",
        163: "Loran's appearance dressed as a woman.\nIt was promoted through Guin's scheme as the pilot of the Turn A Gundam, but it seems that Guin's own personal tastes came through more strongly.\nUnder Kiel's guidance, thorough training as a noble lady was conducted, not just in appearance but also in bearing and dancing. Loran carried it out admirably, even going so far as to capture Harry's heart (?).\nAlthough her appearances in the main story were few, she appeared every time in the first opening sequence.",
        164: "The eldest daughter of the Heim family, whom Loran served as a servant. Age 17.\nShe was not bound by feudal social conventions, held the belief that women should advance into society, and served as Guin's assistant.\nShe resembled Dianna, the Queen of the Moon, so closely that even her own family could not tell them apart. At Dianna's suggestion, they playfully swapped places, but they missed the timing to switch back, and she ended up truly placed in the position of queen.\nHowever, this became a turning point, as she learned that the Moonrace were no different from Earthlings, and she began to make efforts to understand Dianna's thinking and to consider what she herself should do.\nHarry, who was the first to notice the swap, risked his life to protect her, and as they shared the secret, she came to harbor feelings for him. The way she confessed her love was that of a girl her age.",
        165: "The head of the Soreil family that rules the Moon, and the Queen of the Moonrace.\nShe is the spiritual pillar of the Moonrace, commanding overwhelming trust and respect.\nHer official age is 19, but having repeated artificial hibernation many times, several hundred years seem to have passed since her birth. During that time, she has visited Earth on several occasions, and those experiences became a major driving force for the return to Earth.\nThrough a chance occurrence, she met Kiel, who had an identical appearance, and out of mischief, they swapped places and lost the opportunity to return to their original positions. But while living among Earth's people as Kiel, she came to hear their true feelings and learned about the true nature of peace and how to achieve it. And at last, she came to know that her true enemy to fight was Agrippa.",
        166: 'Milan Rex served as a governor who descended to Earth alongside Dianna, acting in a deputy-like capacity. He was believed to be a gentle and intellectual man, but when Phil rebelled in an attempt to seize control of the Dianna Counter, Milan sided with the military. This appeared to be a painful decision made to address various problems, including the slow-moving diplomacy and food shortages. Loyalty to Dianna remained rooted deep in his heart, and when Dianna returned to Earth, he once again became her subject.',
        167: "Sochie Heim was the second daughter of the Heim family, for whom Loran worked as a servant. She was 15 years old. Her personality was competitive, spirited, and boyish. Although she was concerned about Loran, her own position and temperament prevented her from being honest about her feelings. To avenge her father, who died in an attack by the Dianna Counter, she volunteered for the Ingressa Militia and became a Kapool pilot. Because of this, she was initially hardened with hatred toward the Moonrace. However, through learning Loran's true identity and the affair with Gavane, who loved her and even proposed to her, she grew greatly as a person.",
        168: "Meschee Kun was born into a family of airplane makers that had run the business since her grandfather's generation, and she herself flew through the skies as an airplane pilot. She was 18 years old. She belonged to the Ingressa Militia's airplane division and had fought since the outbreak of war. She had a friendship that could be called close with Sochie, and after the Kapool was excavated, the two often rode into battle together. When she went to the Moon, she became friendly with a boy soldier of the Dianna Counter and sortied together with him in a WaD.",
        169: "Corin Nander was a sergeant in the Dianna Counter. In the past, he had been subjected to a freezing sentence in a military prison along with his Eagail for the reason that he had massacred 85 rebel elements who had tried to kill Dianna without holding a trial. As his actions made clear, his loyalty to Dianna was twice as strong as that of others. He was released under the pretext of a pardon to participate in the Earth Return Operation and descended to Earth. However, this was believed to have been arranged by Agrippa, who sought to throw the front lines into confusion by sending the reckless Corin in. Due to the freezing and errors during thawing, his hair had fallen out and part of his face had become altered, but it was said that he had originally been a handsome man with blond hair. He showed an abnormal obsession and hostility toward 'Gundam' and continued to target the Turn A Gundam.",
        170: "Corin Nander was a former sergeant of the Dianna Counter. After being defeated by Loran, he entered the priesthood and wandered the land, but upon seeing the light of the M-Fly released by Merrybell's Turn A Gundam, he remembered his own mission. He then went to Dianna, and when he was permitted to return to the military and to destroy the Turn-type Gundam, he was so overcome with emotion that he shed tears. His unrestrained behavior, such as having a Kapool repainted in his own private colors, continued to astonish those around him. However, his skill had not declined, and he performed aerial combat in a Kapool, which should have been unfamiliar to him, overwhelming the Mahiroo unit with his exploits.",
        171: "is a young man who works on excavation operations in the Mountain Cycle as a disciple of the prospector Sid. He is 23 years old.\nHe was born into the minority Maban tribe, and as a child his parents were killed in tribal warfare. He was abandoned in the mountains and taken in by Sid. Because of this background, he harbored a rivalry that could be called hostility toward the Northern Ameliaans and the Moonrace, and his attitude toward Loran in particular was harsh.\nHis extensive knowledge of machinery was recognized, and he joined the Militia's mobile suit unit, where he came to command the Jarapi (junk car) squad.\nWhile riding in the Flat that Loran and the others used during their descent to Earth, he fought in it, and he gradually developed a close relationship with Fran, who had taught him how to pilot it.",
        172: 'is an old man known as a prospector, an excavator, and also a researcher of the Black History.\nTogether with his disciple Joseph, he excavates machines such as the Kapool from the Mountain Cycle. Through his involvement in commanding the excavation of weapons, he came to accompany the Militia.\nHe showed vitality beyond his years in many places, dashing between excavation sites without sparing time for sleep, and when manpower was short, boarding a Borjarnon to intercept the enemy.\nHis trademark was a helmet with an attached flashlight, reminiscent of a frog, that seemed convenient for excavation work.',
        173: "is the grandson of the lord of Ingressa and the central figure of the Ingressa Militia. He is 19 years old.\nThough raised as a pampered young master, he had no sense of being naive about the world. He showed shrewdness in using whatever was available to him, and talent in negotiation, politics, and judgment, and these were further honed through battle.\nEven when confronted with the Moonrace's overwhelming technology, he was not crushed, but instead secretly planned to use that technology to bring about an industrial revolution. Even when Ingressa fell and he lost power, he resolved to climb back up from there, making him an ambitious man with resilience.\nHe had a strong fixation on Loran, calling him 'Laura' and having him dress in women's clothing.",
        174: "is the commander of the Ingressa Militia. His rank is colonel. He is 35 years old.\nHe believes that the Moonrace are invaders of Earth and that the fight against them is a matter of defending his homeland. For this reason, he seemed displeased with Guin, whom he considered a mere figurehead and who viewed war as nothing more than one means of negotiation.\nHowever, he was swept along by the rapidly changing situation and by Guin's resourcefulness in forming strategies to match, and in the end he followed him all the way to the final battle.",
        175: "Gavane Gooney is the captain of the Suisai Squad, the elite mobile suit unit of the Rujana Militia. He is 27 years old.\nHe has a cheerful personality, but on the battlefield he is a fierce commander who always leads from the front, earning him deep trust from his subordinates. He thinks flexibly, changing tactics to suit the situation.\nWhen he first met the Ingressa Militia, he treated Loran and the others with contempt, calling them 'Ingressa bastards' and challenging the Turn A Gundam to a test of strength. But as they fought together, he came to acknowledge them as comrades in arms. In particular, he was drawn to Sochie, whom he called 'little miss,' by her earnest way of fighting, and he eventually went so far as to propose to her.",
        176: "Lily Borjarnon is the 13th and youngest daughter of Duke Borjarnon, the lord of the Lujane domain. Her personality is selfish and naive, and her carefree attitude of not understanding war is exactly that of a young lady. However, her insight into matters and her observational ability to judge a person's true nature are extraordinary. She has known Guin since childhood, and there were scenes where she harassed Kiel (Dianna) for approaching him. However, she eventually came to admire Kiel, who served as Queen of the Moon in Dianna's place, and offered to become her friend.",
        177: "Horace Niven is a Moonrace engineer. Initially he acted alongside the Dianna Counter that accompanied him, but he defected to Earth, driven by his intellectual curiosity toward the excavated Earth weapons. Thereafter, at Guin's request, he came to cooperate with the Ingressa Militia. There were many places where he could demonstrate his abilities, such as the research, analysis, repair, and maintenance of excavated weapons including the Turn A Gundam. Although most Earthlings did not look favorably upon the Moonrace engineers, they seemed not to care much, perhaps because they were only interested in unknown technology. He had a distinctive face like a Great Buddha statue, and Merrybell, whose face resembled a panda's, told him he had an 'amusing face.'",
        178: "Harry Ord serves as captain of the Dianna Counter's elite guard. He is 18 years old and holds the rank of lieutenant. His personality is calm and intellectual, but because he is overly earnest, he also has an inflexible side. He has sworn absolute loyalty to Dianna, and the depth of his devotion is so famous that even an ordinary female soldier knows of it. He was the first to notice the swap between Dianna and Kiel, but he continued to serve without changing his attitude and protected Kiel. He always wears red sunglasses, which are night-vision goggles, and according to him, they serve to 'hide his gaze when looking at women other than Dianna.' He did not even remove them when kissing Kiel, who had developed feelings for him, but it seems he was not disliked for that. His skill piloting his gold-colored custom SUMO is top-class. At the Winter Palace, he took on the Mahiroo squad led by Suesson and defeated them in seconds with a single unit, which shows his true ability. He favored suits and vests in a yellow-and-black combination, and pajamas with star marks, leaving his fashion sense open to question.",
        179: "Meme Midgard is a Moonrace who infiltrated Earth on Agrippa's orders. His rank is captain. While serving as the manager of Keith's bread factory as a cover, he plotted the assassination of Dianna and the seizure of the Turn A Gundam. He had a sly and suspicious personality, and when he judged that Teteth, whom he had ordered to assassinate Dianna, had failed her mission, he shot her dead to silence her. The marksmanship he displayed at that time was considerable. Furthermore, after returning to the Moon, he resorted to outrageous acts such as fighting a battle that involved the Winter Palace, where many citizens were in cryogenic sleep. However, that action became the trigger for activating the M-Fly.",
        180: "Teteth Halle is a woman who plotted to assassinate Dianna under Midgard's orders. She was born between a Moonrace and a woman whom Dianna had once brought back from Earth to the Moon. Because she was raised with discrimination from a young age, she harbored intense hatred toward everything around her, including Dianna, the lunar system, and her Earthling blood. As a reward for the assassination, she had secured a promise from Midgard to make her an honorary citizen of the Moon.",
        181: "Phil Ackermann was a lieutenant in the Dianna Counter and became the commander of the Earth descent operation after the death of his predecessor. He looked down on Earthlings as barbarians and advocated for subjugation by force. However, taking advantage of Dianna's departure from Earth while she sought peaceful coexistence, he rose in rebellion and declared the founding of the Sunbelt Republic. At one point he even displayed the ambition of becoming the king of Earth, but in the end he swore his loyalty to Dianna once again. He then united with the Earth side, despite lingering ill feelings, and fought against the Ghingnham fleet.",
        182: "Poe Eiji was a lieutenant in the Dianna Counter. She descended to Earth as a pilot of a Wodom under Phil's command. Her interception of the Militia's airplane forces became the opening of the long conflict between Earth and the Moon. She was quick to tears, weeping at every turn, and her tearfulness even became the subtitle of episode 31. She appears to have been in a romantic relationship with her superior Phil, and she followed him when he rebelled against Dianna. Yet, deep in her heart, her loyalty to the queen remained rooted, and when Dianna returned, she wept tears of joy.",
        183: "Ghingnham Gym was the head of the Ghingnham family, which governed the martial arts of the Moonrace, and the supreme commander of the Ghingnham space fleet. True to his words that 'battle itself is my reason for existence,' he always carried a sword and personally boarded the Turn X to go to the front lines. This behavior stemmed from his intense pride in being a man of the warrior class. Ordinarily he held a calm and broad-minded view, but once battle began, he revealed his arrogant and belligerent nature. As a result, he would become so excited that he lost sight of his surroundings and would attack friend and foe alike, exposing his battle mania. His greatest reason for opposing Dianna was his resentment that she had organized the Dianna Counter on her own and descended to Earth, ignoring those like himself who had spent 2,500 years repeating drills. Conversely, this also proved that he held strong loyalty toward Dianna.",
        184: "Suesson Sterro was the captain leading the Mahiroo squad of the Ghingnham fleet. He was rough in temperament, vulgar in character, and casually imposed unreasonable demands on his subordinates. Midgard's assessment of him as 'a water blister leaning on the prestige of a distinguished family' was apt, as he was a man full of flaws. His fighting style also lacked flexibility, as he could only perform formulaic movements due to having conducted nothing but drills within the fleet.",
        185: "Merrybell Gadget was a girl said to be Ghingnham's puppet. She came from the lowest class of the Moon and had been picked up by Ghingnham in the past. Her appearance - a bizarre outfit that also served as a spacesuit, large earmuffs, eye makeup, and bells on her head - along with her agility, such as performing handstands even on Earth with its six times the Moon's gravity, evoked the image of a clown. She preferred to be near capable and amusing individuals such as Ghingnham and Guin, and she would throw out words and actions that incited war toward them. Despite what her demeanor suggested, she possessed exceptional mobile suit piloting skill and maneuvered the Bandit as if it were an extension of her own limbs. Her coordination with unmanned mobile suits seemed to rely on a special ability she possessed, but the details remained unknown.",
        186: 'Agrippa Maintener is the head of the Maintener family, which has managed the Winter Palace, the artificial hibernation facility of the Moonrace. As the administrative official in charge of the internal affairs of Ghingnham, the capital of the Moon, he is well-versed in the Turn A Gundam and the Black History.\nHe had set the maintenance of tranquility and peace in lunar society as his supreme objective, and feared that contact with Earthlings would awaken the instinct for conflict in the hearts of the Moonrace. For this reason, he opposed the Earth descent operation, and carried out various acts of sabotage, such as delaying supplies and plotting the assassination of Dianna.',
        187: "Keith Laijie is a Moonrace youth of 17 who descended to Earth two years ago along with Loran and Fran as an advance surveyor for the return to Earth.\nHe was working as an apprentice at the Donkey bakery in Nox. However, when the Dianna Counter descended, he took over the shop along with the master's daughter Berlune after the master was injured.\nHe sold the flat he had used during the descent to the Ingressa Militia, used the money to build a bread factory, and actively hired Moonrace who had fled. This positive attitude of doing his best at what he could do greatly contributed to bridging Earth and the Moon at the civilian level.\nWhether as a result of his efforts or not, his bread-making skill was excellent, and its taste was highly praised by both Earthlings and Moonrace alike.",
        188: 'Fran Doll is a Moonrace girl of 17 who descended to Earth two years ago along with Loran and Keith as an advance surveyor for the return to Earth.\nShe worked as a printer at the Nox Chronicle, a Nox newspaper company, but later became a newspaper reporter, fulfilling her long-held wish. She always considered the significance of reporting and tried to convey the truth without flinching even in the face of war. Even when she learned that her articles were being suppressed by media controls, she did not abandon her duties as a reporter.\nShe came to know Joseph through a chance encounter, and eventually became close enough to speak her true feelings and act dependent in front of him.',
        189: "Garrod Ran is a boy of 15 who survives in the devastated world by his own strength without relying on others.\nHe is a war orphan, but has a bright and forward-looking personality that shows no sense of tragedy. Perhaps because his father was a military scientist, he is skilled in handling machinery in general. Behind that may have been a desire to become an engineer like his father. Before boarding the Freeden, he used his natural resourcefulness and cunning to hunt Mobile Suits and sell them to junk dealers, living toughly. Perhaps learned from such a life, he once opened the locks of the Freeden and the Bradman residence using only wire.\nHis Mobile Suit piloting skill was genius-level, and he quickly mastered the Gundam X and the Gundam Double X on his first flights. Even in his first battle in space, he grasped the knack in an extremely short time. Lancelow, who witnessed his high adaptability, could not hide his astonishment.\nDuring a certain job, he met the Newtype girl Tiffa and fell in love at first sight. From then on, he continued to show single-minded devotion, plunging into fire, water, sea, or space without regard for danger if it was for her sake.\nThough self-proclaimed, the epithet 'Pilot of the Flaming Mobile Suit' accurately describes him, for better or worse.",
        190: "Tiffa Adill is a naturally awakened Newtype girl of 15, born after the 7th Space War, who was whispered to be impossible. She exhibits powers that could be called psychic abilities, such as future sight, danger detection, and heightened perception (the Newtypes of 'Gundam X' differ in meaning from the Newtypes of previous Gundam series).\nMany organizations targeted her as research material for these abilities, and she was rescued by Jamil and the others from confinement in a Newtype research facility. After boarding the Freeden, she became the group's guide and ultimately reached the D.O.M.E. on the Moon.\nAlthough her Newtype abilities were sought after by those around her, she herself feared them. She also detested people fighting over this power, and so lived with her heart half-closed. However, she gradually opened up to Garrod, who treated her as an ordinary girl, and eventually came to express her feelings outwardly.\nIn the midst of battle, she wished to be of help to Garrod and other precious people, and the power heightened by that feeling became a factor in opening the D.O.M.E. on the Moon.",
        191: "Jamil Neate is the captain of the Freeden, a ship dedicated to the search and protection of Newtypes. He is 30 years old.\nIn addition to not showing his emotions, the sunglasses he always wears give him an even more taciturn impression. However, the crew of the Freeden place immense trust in their captain, revealing his human charm.\nDuring the 7th Space War, he belonged to the Earth Federation Forces and was a Newtype who served as the pilot of the Gundam X. But in the final phase of the war, he pulled the trigger that became the catalyst for the greatest tragedy in human history, the 'Colony Drop'. That guilt became a trauma, and he lost all of his Newtype abilities.\nHe suffered from a fear of cockpits that developed from his trauma, but he overcame it through his encounter with Garrod. Thereafter, he piloted the Gundam X Divider and played an active role.",
        192: 'Sara Tyrrell is the operator of the Freeden. She is 18 years old.\nShe is a woman in a vice-captain position who sometimes serves as acting captain when Jamil is absent.\nShe takes a theoretical approach to thinking and acts accordingly, but at times she could not suppress her own emotions and would speak harshly.\nShe harbors feelings beyond respect for Jamil, and when it comes to him, she cannot remain calm. She was also seen showing jealousy toward Tiffa, who was still a girl. Amidst that, Roybea made advances toward her, and she found herself torn between him and Jamil.',
        193: "Toniya Malme is the communications officer of the Freeden. She is 17 years old.\nShe has a bright and friendly personality, and she serves as the mood maker not only on the bridge but throughout the entire Freeden.\nShe was bound by a deep friendship with Ennil, whom she met during their journey, and her inherent brightness became a major catalyst for thawing Ennil's closed heart. However, her blunt way of speaking sometimes hurt others, and she once made a careless remark about Witz's photograph, touching on a deep wound.\nBut that incident became a turning point, and she gradually grew closer to Witz. Then, before the final battle, they had become close enough that he gave her a ring along with his feelings.",
        194: 'Shingo Mori is the helmsman of the Freeden. He is 20 years old.\nHis appearance is plain, and his presence is somewhat lacking. However, his skill at the helm is first-rate, making him an indispensable presence on the Freeden. When he first went to space, he demonstrated a masterful feat by handling the helm of the Freeden II after merely reading the manual.\nWhile at anchor, he also handles various miscellaneous duties, and when Garrod, who had infiltrated the Freeden, was put in a cell, he served as the guard.',
        195: 'Witz Sou is a mobile suit pilot hired by the Freeden. He is 17 years old.\nHe has a manly personality in every sense, and he is the type who acts before he speaks. His language is also quite rough.\nHe was originally a freelance mobile suit pilot, and the Gundam Air Master was a keepsake from a Vulture who had taken care of him in the past. Initially, he gave the impression of a money-grubber who fought only for pay, but that was all to make life easier for his family back home.\nHis father had been killed by a mobile suit pilot in the past, and while he agonized over not being able to reveal his job to his mother, who hated that profession, he possessed the kindness to keep fighting for his family.\nHe eventually signed an exclusive contract with the Freeden, with which he had various connections. Witz rationalized it by saying that the Freeden was suitable as a hiding place for the gold he earned, but it is thought that one of the reasons was that he wanted to be near Toniya, for whom he had secretly developed feelings.',
        196: "Roybea Loy is a mobile suit pilot employed by the Freeden. 18 years old. As a freelance mobile suit pilot, he maintains a carefree and self-indulgent attitude, saying 'I hate things that are too ideological.' However, when the Freeden, which had previously employed him, fell into crisis, he rushed to its aid, and as he himself says, he is 'actually a good guy.' He eventually signed an exclusive contract with the Freeden, which he had various ties to, and began to act alongside it. At that time, he tried to set up a relaxation room on the ship and collect membership fees from the crew. However, under Sara's conditions, women were free, and no money could be collected from children (under 15), so Garrod and Tiffa were also free, and after losing a billiards match, Tex was free as well, meaning he ended up providing the room for free to almost everyone who would use it. He is flirtatious and frivolous, skilled with both his hands and his tongue, and his hobby is seducing women. He has lovers in various places, and he is diligent enough to find time to visit them under the pretext of aftercare. However, the woman he truly loved has already passed away, and his beloved Gundam Leopard is her memento. His current true love is Sara. He seems to harbor surprisingly sincere feelings for her and constantly makes advances on her.",
        197: 'Ennil El is a freelance mobile suit pilot whose beloved machine is always painted blue. 19 years old. Using her skill and beauty, she has survived alone in the postwar world. Because she has lived a harsh life driven by mere survival, she has built a wall that keeps others from getting close to her heart. She met Garrod when he took the Gundam X from the Freeden, and after he rejected her seduction, her pride was wounded, and she subsequently chased after him in a state of misplaced resentment. Later, she met Toniya, who was in town during shore leave, and through deepening their friendship as women, a change occurred in her feelings. Afterwards, her life was saved by the Freeden, and from then on she came to cooperate with Garrod as well.',
        198: 'Kid Salsamill is the chief mechanic of the Freeden. As the youngest crew member at 12 years old, he serves as chief, which shows that his mechanical skill and knowledge rival those of an adult. Besides maintaining mobile suits, he is quite versatile, creating simulators for Bit attacks and adjusting the combination mechanism of the G-Falcon. Jamil never interferes with his work, indicating that he places great trust in him. He constantly hoards useful parts and ideas, and it was his handiwork that powered up the various Gundam units, including the Gundam X, the Airmaster, and the Leopard.',
        199: "Tex Farzenberg is the exclusive physician of the Freeden. 36 years old. His ability as a doctor is extremely high, and he handles all kinds of work, from internal medicine to surgery, as well as psychological care. As the oldest crew member, he possesses deep experience and the composure of an adult. Jamil trusts him deeply and often consulted with him. He is a voracious reader and once recited the contents of 'Lorelei' by the German poet Heine. His hobby is billiards, and his skill in that area is considerable, as he won decisively in a match against Roybea with the usage fee for the relaxation room at stake. Later, when most of the crew went out for supplies, he tried to take the opportunity to do secret training, but was flustered when Sara and Toniya witnessed the scene, revealing an unexpectedly childlike side.",
        200: "Pala Sys is a pilot of the G-Falcon, belonging to the resistance organization Satelicon against the Space Revolutionary Army. 15 years old. She lost both parents, who were space refugees, soon after her birth. Having grown up in an environment surrounded by men, her language is rough, and she often blurts out things like 'That's lame.' Her personality is also as masculine as possible, but when Satelicon was destroyed, tears of sorrow, and after achieving the destruction of the colonial laser that was her true goal, tears of joy streamed down her cheeks. At that moment, her face was that of a girl her age. She hit it off with Garrod when she saved him from a pinch in space, and they came to fight together. Afterwards, when she joined the Freeden, she got along well with Kid, who was a kindred spirit.",
        201: "Shagia Frost is the elder of the notorious Frost brothers, free mobile suit pilots. He is 19 years old. His appearance as a free mobile suit pilot is a cover; his true identity is an agent of the New Federation's intelligence agency. He possesses the telepathic ability 'Twins' Synchronity,' which allows him to communicate with his fraternal twin brother Olba without words. This enables them to avoid danger for each other and to conduct operations even from distant locations. However, despite such abilities, they were not recognized under the supremacy of Newtypes and were branded with the 'Category F' label. As a result, he came to hate Newtypes and everything in the world that acknowledged their existence. His personality is cruel and ruthless, and he stops at nothing to achieve his goals. He killed his targets of revenge and those who had outlived their usefulness one after another, sometimes with his beloved Gundam Virsago and sometimes by directly pointing a gun at them. He was always calm and composed, able to accurately assess the surrounding situation and the tide of battle. He often admonished Olba, whose blood would rush to his head and lose sight of the situation.",
        202: "Olba Frost is the younger of the notorious Frost brothers, free mobile suit pilots. He is 19 years old. His appearance as a free mobile suit pilot is a cover; his true identity is an agent of the New Federation's intelligence agency. He possesses the telepathic ability 'Twins' Synchronity,' which allows him to communicate with his fraternal twin brother Shagia without words. This enables them to avoid danger for each other and to conduct operations even from distant locations. However, despite such abilities, they were not recognized under the supremacy of Newtypes and were branded with the 'Category F' label. As a result, he came to hate Newtypes and everything in the world that acknowledged their existence. His personality is cold and heartless, and he stops at nothing to achieve his goals. But that was only his outward face; hidden within his refined features was a passion beyond imagination. He was often restrained by Shagia when his blood rushed to his head and he lost sight of the situation.",
        203: "Lancerow Dawell is the captain of the Space Revolutionary Army's training battalion, with the rank of colonel. He is 34 years old. During the 7th Space War, he was a Newtype who fought evenly with Jamil, but after the war ended, he lost that ability. Even 15 years later, he remains with the Revolutionary Army and is highly favored by President Seidel. However, he is aware that this is because, as a former Newtype, he holds value to the populace as a symbol of the future and to the military as a means to boost morale. Even without his Newtype powers, his mobile suit piloting skills are top-notch. When he clashed with Garrod, who went to space for Tiffa, he overwhelmed him with ease, as if twisting a baby's arm. Eventually, he learned that Jamil was fighting to protect Newtypes, came to understand his actions, and lent aid to Jamil and his group when they were struggling against the Frost brothers.",
        204: 'Katock Alzamille is a soldier belonging to the New Federation. His abilities as a soldier are high enough to serve as captain of a special unit, but he is also a man who causes trouble in various places, such as disobeying orders and firing at superiors. He infiltrated the Freeden disguised as a fisherman, intending to capture it, but failed and was instead taken prisoner. Later, amid the chaos of battle, he seized the bridge and achieved his objective, but meeting Tiffa brought a change to his heart. When Garrod sought to rescue Tiffa, who had been captured by the New Federation, he cooperated without regard for his own interests. Though he claimed to dislike it, he often spoke of his dead wife whenever something happened, revealing the depth of his feelings for the family he had lost in the war.',
        205: "Seidel Rasso is the president of the Space Revolutionary Army. He advocated the ideology of Newtype supremacy, holding that 'humanity is truly established as Newtypes only through space transforming them,' and sought to lead humanity living in space. However, these claims were nothing more than a pretext to maintain his own power, and he did not truly need Newtypes. For that reason, he stubbornly refused to acknowledge Tiffa, a naturally occurring Newtype born and raised on Earth. While he was in the midst of a decisive battle on the Moon to destroy the New Federation and obtain the power of Newtypes, he was led to D.O.M.E. and came into contact with its true essence.",
        206: "The supreme commander of the New Federation Forces. He feared that with the rise of Newtypes, all people including himself would be branded as old humanity. He was flattered by the Frost Brothers as 'one destined to become the new leader of the world,' and eventually, guided by them, he would engage in a decisive battle with the revolutionary army on the Moon.",
        207: "A fifteen-year-old boy serving as the leader of the self-defense corps in the regional city of Fort Severn. He was an artificial Newtype so excellent that Mayor Nomoa called him 'my greatest masterpiece.' He himself possessed absolute confidence in his own power, and had the ability to match it. He repelled the Gundam X with his beloved Vertigo, but the existence of Tiffa, a natural Newtype who should not have existed, and his defeat at the hands of the revived Garrod caused him to lose his sense of purpose. Finally, when he tried to take his own life, Garrod saved him, and that event opened his heart. Afterwards, his power was exploited by Nomoa, who was actually Dorat, and he destroyed the city with the Patulia. After Dorat was defeated by Garrod and the others, he resolved to devote himself to rebuilding the city as atonement. Later, as a unit commander leading a force of the anti-New Federation organization, he saved the crew of the Freeden from a crisis. Furthermore, when they needed a means to reach space, he even provided a space battleship.",
        208: "A former Federation forces educational officer and instructor in charge of the Flash System. She was Jamil's superior during his military days, but to him she was a woman of greater significance than that. In the final stages of the great war, her hatred of battle and her wish for peace grew too strong, causing her to suffer a mental breakdown. The Federation Forces, noticing her Newtype abilities and her hatred of fighting, used her as the core of the L System, which could disable the electronic equipment of weapons. However, the L Operation that was supposed to employ it was ultimately cancelled. The L System later lay at the bottom of the sea, but it was discovered and recovered during the salvage of the G Bits that had sunk alongside it. The Lucile within was not completely unconscious; she appeared before Jamil using Tiffa's body and saved the Freeden from an attack by the Sea Barchew. She also lent her power to Jamil, who had lost his Newtype abilities, and assisted in controlling the G Bits. After the battle ended, she was reunited with Jamil.",
        209: 'The intelligence chief of the Government Rebuilding Committee. He was the man who had the Gundam Double X developed on Zonder Epta Island. He focused on Newtypes, plotting to gain their power and take control of the committee. He believed he was manipulating the Frost Brothers to suit his own purposes, but in reality he was merely being used by them.',
        210: 'A military officer belonging to the New Federation Forces, with the rank of lieutenant. He was originally a skilled pilot, but during combat with Garrod he awakened the Newtype abilities he had latent potential for, and used Bit mobile suit tactics to drive Garrod and the others into a corner.',
        211: "Shinn Asuka is a mobile suit pilot assigned to the Minerva. He is 16 years old.\nBorn and raised in Orb, he lived peacefully with his family, unaware of war. However, during the Earth Alliance's invasion of Orb in the previous war, he lost both his parents and his younger sister before his very eyes. Shortly thereafter, at Todaka's suggestion, he relocated to PLANT, and, believing that 'power is necessary to protect what is precious,' he joined ZAFT. He graduated from the academy with excellent records and rose to wear the red uniform, the mark of an elite pilot. Given this background, while his nature is cheerful, he has a very sensitive side, and his aggression often comes to the surface.\nHis hidden potential was recognized by Durandal, and he was chosen as the pilot of the Impulse Gundam, the latest mobile suit. When the three Second Stage Gundams were stolen, he sortied to take them back. Initially, due to a lack of combat experience, he achieved little, but eventually, his rejection of the repeated battles and deaths caused him to awaken SEED. From then on, he fought with unparalleled vigor and grew into a top ace. While he respected Athrun, he often vented his anger at Athrun's indecisive attitude.\nHis chance encounter with Stella, and their reunion amid battle, led him to see the shadow of his younger sister in her. When Stella was taken prisoner, he risked his own life to let her escape, but even so, she could not be saved from her cruel fate.",
        212: "Ray Za Barrel is a mobile suit pilot assigned to the Minerva.\nHe is always calm, possesses excellent situational judgment, and his mobile suit piloting skills surpass those of his peers Shinn and Lunamaria. In space, he fought evenly with Neo, and his abilities were recognized by those around him to the extent that Arthur wondered, 'Why was the Impulse given to Shinn and not Ray?'\nHe adores Durandal, and in his presence, his personality changes into that of an innocent boy. At times, however, his absolute trust appeared fanatical.\nHe viewed the Archangel, which did not obey Durandal, as an enemy, and his conflict with Athrun, who could not sever his past ties with them, deepened.",
        213: 'Lunamaria Hawke is a mobile suit pilot assigned to the Minerva. She is 17 years old.\nAlong with Shinn and Ray, she achieved excellent results at the academy and became a member of the elite known as the red uniforms. She primarily fought in a GOUF Ignited painted in her personal color, red.\nTogether with her younger sister Meyrin, she took an interest in Athrun, the hero of the previous war, and made various advances toward him. However, she was greatly shocked by a certain action taken by Athrun and Meyrin.',
        214: "Talia Gladys is the captain of ZAFT's new warship, the Minerva. She is 29 years old.\nAs befitting one of ZAFT's rare female captains, she excels in situational judgment and in managing people, and she kept the young crew, including Shinn and the others, well organized.\nIn the past, she and Durandal had been lovers, but because she could not bear his child due to incompatibility, she was forced to end their relationship. Even so, it seems that lingering feelings remain on both sides.\nFrom the time of the LOGOS subjugation onward, she grew increasingly distrustful of the unreasonable orders and inexplicable behavior handed down by Durandal.",
        215: "Arthur Trine is the deputy captain of ZAFT's new warship, the Minerva. He is 26 years old.\nDespite holding the important post of deputy captain, he is timid and restless. He tends to get carried away, and so was frequently reprimanded by Talia.\nHe treated the veteran crew members such as Shinn and Ray with familiarity, but he often cast a cold eye on Athrun, who joined midway.",
        216: 'Meyrin Hawke is a crew member of the ZAFT new battleship Minerva, in charge of communications control and search operations. She is 16 years old.\nAlong with her older sister Lunamaria, she takes an interest in Athrun, a hero of the previous war. She is also skilled at operating information terminals, and has used that skill to research information on Athrun.\nAs she watches Athrun become isolated within the ship, she gradually comes to feel complex emotions that go beyond mere admiration. Eventually, she takes a bold action that shocks those around her.',
        217: 'Yolant Kent is a mechanic on the Minerva. He is 17 years old.\nHe is a classmate and friend of Ray and Meyrin from the academy. Unlike his partner Vino, he has a serious personality and is a big fan of Lacus.',
        218: 'Vino Duple is a mechanic on the Minerva. He is 16 years old.\nHe is a classmate and friend of Shin and Lunamaria from the academy. Unlike his partner Yolant, he has a light and cheerful personality. He is especially close to Shin.',
        219: 'Alex Dino is the false name Athrun used when he defected to Orb after the end of the previous war. His disguise consists of no more than wearing sunglasses when going out, so it is not hard to imagine that anyone who knows him would see through it at a glance.',
        220: "Athrun Zala is one of the figures who brought the previous war to an end, and is a hero whose name is known to everyone in PLANT. He is 18 years old.\nAfter the war, he defected to Orb and served as the bodyguard of his lover Cagalli. However, faced with the war that began anew, he was forced to taste the helplessness of being unable to do anything. In that state, Durandal invited him, and after bidding farewell to Cagalli, he rejoined ZAFT as a member of the special forces FAITH.\nRiding the Savior Gundam entrusted to him upon rejoining, he fought as a member of the Minerva's crew, but eventually came into conflict with Kira and the others over differences in opinion.\nAt first he sympathized with Durandal's ideals, but after the suspicion surrounding Lacus's assassination, the use of the fake Meer, and the order to attack the Archangel, which should have shared the same purpose, he gradually grew more distrustful.",
        221: "Athrun Zala, who escaped from ZAFT, resolved to fight alongside Kira and the others once more. Facing Durandal's 'Destiny Plan,' he has officially become a member of the Orb military.\nThe hesitation he once felt, torn between what he believed in and what he wanted to believe in, is now gone. Furthermore, by obtaining the  Justice Gundam, which carries on the lineage of his former beloved mobile suit, he is now able to fully display his true combat capabilities.",
        222: "A crew member of the Archangel and the pilot of the Freedom Gundam. He is 18 years old. In addition to genetic adjustment, he is the product of various experiments, a being that could be called a 'Super Coordinator.'\nIn the previous war, as a third power, he fought against both the Earth Alliance and PLANT, leading the war to its conclusion. Afterward, he went into exile in Orb with Murrue, who had fought alongside him, and his lover Lacus, living a life far removed from battle. However, witnessing the fall of Junius Seven and the battle against the assassination squad sent after Lacus made him strongly feel the need to stop the expanding flames of war. At last, he initiated military action together with his former comrades.\nHis combat ability is so high that no one else can match him. Yet, because of his overly gentle personality, which abhors conflict and killing, he strives to fight without killing opponents, destroying only weapons and cameras even in battle. This eventually becomes his undoing, and he is once defeated by Shinn's desperate attack. But later, he is revived by obtaining new wings, the Strike Freedom Gundam.",
        223: "The representative of the Orb Union chief state. She is 18 years old.\nShe carries on the will of the former representative Uzumi, striving to lead her homeland and the world to peace. However, due to her youth and inexperience, as well as the covert machinations of the Seiran father and son, she cannot unite the nation, and she keenly feels her own powerlessness.\nWhen Athrun, with whom she had been in love since the previous war, left Orb, he gave her a ring. However, afterward, for the reason of 'unifying the nation,' she reluctantly decided to marry Yuna, and she cut off her feelings. But during the wedding ceremony, she was taken away by her twin brother Kira's Freedom Gundam, and the marriage was ruined.",
        224: "The captain of the Archangel. She is 28 years old. For convenience, her rank is listed as Commander (Lieutenant Commander) from her Earth Alliance days.\nDuring the previous war, she was originally a member of the Earth Alliance, but she defected midway due to doubts about the military's actions. As a third power, she was a driving force in bringing the previous war to an end. Though she sometimes makes cold-hearted decisions, she is essentially a kind woman who has watched over her young crew like a mother.\nAfter the war, she went to Orb with Kira, Waltfeld, Lacus, and others who had fought alongside her, and she worked in the shipbuilding section of Morgenroete Corporation. Just as she was considering moving to PLANT, she was attacked by a special forces unit plotting Lacus's assassination, but she barely managed to repel them. That incident prompted her to decide to launch the Archangel for the sake of a world once again falling into chaos.\nDuring the battle at Berlin, she had a tragic reunion with her lover, who had supposedly died shielding the Archangel in the previous war, and she shed tears of sorrow.",
        225: 'The helmsman of the Archangel. He is 27 years old. His nominal rank is Ensign (Lieutenant Junior Grade) from his Earth Alliance days.\nAfter the previous war, he seems to have lived as a civilian in Orb. Even so, navigating the Archangel skillfully on land, underwater, and in space, as well as performing evasive maneuvers during combat, he proved his skill remained intact. The fact that he could fight on equal terms or better against the new warship Minerva was largely due to his helmsmanship.\nAfter Cagalli returned to Orb, he was formally incorporated into the Orb military along with the other members.',
        226: 'A controller aboard the Archangel, responsible for search, radar, and fire control. 26 years old. For convenience, his rank is listed as a sergeant from his time in the Earth Alliance Forces. His whereabouts after the previous war were unknown, and as can be seen from the lack of any particular return scene, he has a faint presence aside from his name. However, he reliably performs his duties, and in the elite, undermanned Archangel, which suffers from a greater shortage of personnel than in the previous war, he is an indispensable existence. After Cagalli returned to Orb, he was formally incorporated into the Orb military along with the other crew members.',
        227: "A crew member of the Archangel in charge of communications control. 18 years old. She was originally just an ordinary student, but was swept up into the military in the previous war. Having lost her lover Tolle on the battlefield, she was at one point consumed by a dark hatred of Coordinators. Yet as she came to learn the hidden side of the war, she grew mentally and fought through to the end of the conflict. After the war's conclusion, she traveled the world as a battlefield journalist, camera in hand, photographing and witnessing wars across the globe. Combined with her own past experiences, she grieved for a world stained by conflict, but when the Archangel launched once more, she boarded the ship again to fight alongside it. After Cagalli rose as head of state, she was formally incorporated into the Orb military.",
        228: "An idol who was once called the 'Songstress of PLANT.' 18 years old. Her presence and charisma were immense, and in the previous war she pointed the way for Kira, Athrun, and others, gathering those who shared her convictions, becoming a great driving force that led the conflict to its end. After the previous war, she crossed to Orb together with Waltfeld, Murrue, and her lover Kira, who had fought alongside her. There she lived quietly with Reverend Malchio, Kira's adoptive mother Caridad, and a group of orphans, but learned that her brief peace had been shattered by the appearance of those who sought to assassinate her. With the emergence of the fake Meer as well, her suspicions toward Durandal deepened. Resolving to return to the public stage, Lacus boarded the Archangel together with Kira.",
        229: "Captain of the high-speed battleship Eternal. 32 years old. He was originally a member of ZAFT, a fierce warrior feared under the epithet 'Desert Tiger.' However, during the previous war he defected from the military, siding with Lacus and helping bring the conflict to an end. After the previous war, he fled to Orb together with Kira, Murrue, Lacus, and the others who had fought alongside him, enjoying a brief peace while savoring his hobby of coffee. While considering a move to PLANT, he was attacked by a special forces unit aiming to assassinate Lacus, and repelled them. Taking that as a turning point, he resolved to once again face the war as a third faction. After the Archangel launched, he supported Murrue in a vice-captain-like position, and in times of crisis sortied in a Murasame painted in his personal colors, displaying that his skills had not diminished. When Lacus later acted to confirm the state of PLANT, he went up into space with her as her escort. When the Eternal resumed operations, he took his old seat in its captain's chair as in the previous war. When forced to fight alone, he also sortied in the Gaia Gundam, successor to his former beloved machine. After Cagalli returned to Orb, he was formally incorporated into the Orb military.",
        230: "Waltfeld's adjutant. He belonged to ZAFT during the previous war, but defected together with Waltfeld and joined the Clyne faction. In place of his superior, he always works faithfully behind the scenes. In the current war as well, he played a significant role, protecting the Eternal while Lacus and the others were away, and discovering notes on the Destiny Plan inside the abandoned colony Mendel.",
        231: 'Kojirou Murdoch is the mechanic chief of the Archangel. He is 33 years old. For convenience, his rank is listed as Sergeant Major from his time in the Earth Alliance Forces.\nAfter the end of the previous war, he appears to have worked at Morgenroete, and he single-handedly handles the maintenance of both mobile suits and the Archangel, which is convincing given his undiminished skill.\nHe is stubborn, foul-mouthed, and gives a rough impression from his appearance. However, his sense of responsibility toward his position as a mechanic, whose work affects the lives of pilots, and the feelings he holds for his comrades that stem from it, are stronger than most. When Athrun attempted to sortie despite his injuries, he contacted Murrue to have her stop him.',
        232: "Yuna Roma Seiran is the heir of the Seiran family, one of Orb's five major clans, and is Cagalli's fiance. He is 22 years old.\nIn collusion with his father Unato, he used smooth talk to carry out a marriage with Cagalli, aiming to take control of Orb in name and in fact. During the wedding ceremony that eventually came, Cagalli was taken from him by Kira's Freedom Gundam. Furthermore, he was interrupted during the subsequent battle with the Minerva, and his pride was thoroughly crushed on every front.\nAfter sitting in the Orb representative's seat due to Cagalli's absence, he went to the front lines as the commander leading the Orb fleet. However, his command ability is completely nonexistent, being utterly childish. Moreover, he was so obsessed with operation names that he cooled the mood of those around him, and even while other crew members worked through the night, he slept soundly alone, making his casual attitude plainly visible.",
        233: "Unato Ema Seiran is the head of the Seiran family, one of Orb's five major clans, and Yuna's father.\nDespite holding the position of chancellor supporting the nation, he plotted to dominate Orb by having Yuna and Cagalli marry.",
        234: "Todaka is the captain of the aircraft carrier Takemikazuchi belonging to the Orb Navy. His rank is Commander (Colonel).\nHe had a warm-hearted personality and good sense, and he enjoyed the deep trust of his subordinates.\nHe constantly harbored resentment toward unreasonable orders, such as attacks on the Minerva, which saved the Earth from Junius Seven's fall, and on the Archangel carrying Cagalli, the head of state. Regarding the reckless order issued by Yuna, who was aboard as supreme commander, to 'attack that Cagalli because she is a fake,' he judged that since Orb had already allied with the Earth Alliance, it was unavoidable in order to protect Orb. Placing his hopes on the Freedom Gundam serving as escort, he issued the attack order with great reluctance.",
        235: "Ledonir Kisaka is a soldier belonging to the Orb Army. His rank is Commander (Colonel).\nHe is a direct subordinate of Uzumi, the former head of state of Orb, and in the previous war he also served as Cagalli's guard. After Uzumi's death, he continued to watch over her as her guardian.\nAfter the alliance between the Earth Alliance and Orb, he infiltrated the Earth Alliance Forces to investigate their movements.",
        236: 'Durandal is the Chairman of the PLANT Supreme Council. He is 32 years old.\nUnlike his predecessor, Chairman Patrick Zala, he is a moderate who seeks a path of coexistence and peace with the Naturals. During the Junius Seven fall incident and the subsequent battles with the Earth Alliance, he consistently made calm and precise judgments, demonstrating excellent leadership.\nHe is also a leading authority on genetic research, and it is thought that he came to know Rau and Ray through that connection. He also seemed to have anticipated from the start that Shinn would manifest the SEED factor.\nHe promoted Meer as Lacus in an attempt to raise the morale of all of PLANT. However, his secret plot to assassinate the real Lacus was exposed, which earned him the opposition of Kira and the others.',
        237: "Yzak is the captain of the ZAFT Joule Team. He is 19 years old.\nDuring the previous war, he cooperated with the Archangel and the Eternal at the very end, and together they contributed to bringing the war to a close.\nAfter the war ended, with Durandal's assistance, he returned to ZAFT, and thanks to his talent, he rose at a young age to the position of team captain. His ability to command his unit using his abundant combat experience, and his skill in battle, are first-rate. He was active across a wide range of operations in space, including helping the Minerva prevent the fall of Junius Seven, defending PLANT from the Earth Alliance's unilateral attacks, and the operation to destroy the beam deflection station when PLANT became a target of Requiem (though this ended in failure).\nWhen he reunited with Athrun, he strongly urged him to rejoin the military, showing that he had grown beyond the petty rivalry he once clung to.",
        238: "Dearka belongs to ZAFT and serves as the adjutant and second-in-command of the Joule Team, led by his best friend Yzak. He is 19 years old.\nHe was also a member of ZAFT during the previous war, but after being taken prisoner, he came aboard the Archangel and fought alongside them. After contributing to ending the war as part of a third faction, he returned to PLANT.\nWhether it is because he was questioned about that incident is uncertain, but he wears the standard soldier's uniform instead of the red uniform that marks an elite. However, his skill as a pilot is in no way diminished, and it can be said that he has grown into a more reliable man, both in ability and in mental fortitude.",
        239: "Heine is a member of the ZAFT special forces unit FAITH. Under Durandal's orders, he was transferred to the Minerva. He is 21 years old.\nWith a bright and friendly personality, he had the adaptability and sociability to immediately blend in with the Minerva's crew despite joining partway through. He particularly looked after Athrun, admonishing him when he saw him troubled over battle, and acting to close the distance between him and Shinn and the others, who had their own walls.\nHis mobile suit piloting skill is also high, and his machine was always painted in his personal color, orange. He distinguished himself in the PLANT defense battle in a ZAKU Phantom, and in the Battle of the Dardanelles in a GOUF Ignited that had been deployed ahead of time.\nIncidentally, in German, 'Westen' means 'west' and 'fluss' means 'river'. This naming was done as a tribute to Heine's voice actor, the artist Takanori Nishikawa, who also performed the theme song.",
        240: 'Meer is a girl discovered by Durandal, who thought that someone was needed to captivate the masses as a stand-in for Lacus after she disappeared from the public eye. She is 17 years old.\nBeing herself a great fan of Lacus, her figure appealing for peace moved the hearts of many, and her singing voice attracted countless people. Thanks to plastic surgery, her appearance and voice were exactly the same as the real thing. However, the tone of her songs and her mannerisms were quite different, which made Yolant and others somewhat suspicious. Even so, in the end, she seemed to have gained popularity approaching that of the real Lacus.\nWhether she was faithfully maintaining the fiction that she was engaged to Athrun, or acting out of genuine affection, she approached him excessively and left him bewildered.',
    },
}
